    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269-a1">

                <pb facs="0780" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg566"/>

                <head>Mr. Peirce to Mr. Harris</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Honolulu,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 29, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Under instructions from the Hon. Hamilton
                    Fish, Secretary of State, I have the honor and pleasure to convey the thanks of
                    the United States Government to His Hawaiian Majesty, and to Mr. Hutchison, his
                    minister of the interior, for the aid and assistance rendered by them to the
                    officers and crew of the United States steamer Saginaw, by the prompt dispatch
                    of the government steamer Kilauea, and the timely and efficient relief afforded
                    to those shipwrecked on Ocean Island; also for the deep interest manifested by
                    His Majesty in the fate of those unfortunate persons.</p>
                <p>Renewing assurances of great consideration and high respect, I am your
                    excellency’s obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HENRY A. PEIRCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency C. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harris,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">His Hawaiian Majesty’s Minister of Foreign
                            Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
